            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "VONDA99"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I am always asked to make this dip for office parties; the recipe I use also includes a layer of salsa on top of the hormel chili, but only one package of cream cheese. This is quick, easy, and delicious."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kate Preston"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I use one package cream cheese, spread into bottom of 8x8 glass pan. Cover with a full tin of Stagg Dynamite Chili (with beans). Cover with grated cheese. Decorate the top with: chopped red peppers, green onions, black olives, pickled or raw jalapeños, your choice. Or none at all. Bake in oven at 350 for 20-30 minutes. It will disappear! A great dish to take to a happy hour or party. Never fails! Been making it for years!",
            "datePublished": "2020-02-23T17:47:17.833Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "dbray"
            },
            "reviewBody": "People were scraping the sides of the crock pot for more - no kidding! Night before, I cooked on stove 2 cans of Stag steak chili(with beans) incorporating the cream cheese until well mixed, took off the heat and added 1/2 cup of shredded cheddar cheese and put away. Next day I put all in a 1 1/2 qt crock pot with a bit of water to keep it from getting to thick, topped with some more shredded cheese and green onion for garnish and served at with Frito scoops and blue corn tortilla chips.",
            "datePublished": "2010-11-16T18:08:31.947Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Angie Mahoney"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious!!! Followed some reviewer tips and layered some salsa, 8 oz cream cheese, just over a cup of homemade turkey chili, salsa, and a bunch of cheese (chihuahua jalapeño and taco blend). Baked at 325 for about 20 minutes until bubbly. So easy! I made this in an 8x8 dish. I’ll look forward to eating leftovers.",
            "datePublished": "2021-02-07T23:56:51.233Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "nvymum"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Like so many others, I have been making this for years. I use just 1 package of cream cheese. I also mix some sliced green and black olives into the chili before putting it on the cream cheese layer. I have tried both baking and microwaving this tasty dip and definitely prefer the baking method-325 degrees for 20-25 minutes. My family likes the \"layered-effect, rather than mixing the chili and cream cheese together.",
            "datePublished": "2018-02-02T04:06:52.247Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "nancy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is an oldie but Goodie, I've made it for 20 yrs. hormel has 1/3 less fat than Wolf brand canned chili!\nI like the idea of chopped green onions in the cream cheese. I bake in 10\" glass pie pan in oven 325 til all melts and serve with crackers. Simple and always eaten up!",
            "datePublished": "2014-01-20T10:07:03.637Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I threw all the ingredients for this into my small \"Little Dipper\" crockpot early this morning, only using the chili I made last night (with black beans) instead of canned beans. I also used reduced fat cream cheese. My three men are already dipping into it and drooling over my countertop. Great weekend treat!",
            "datePublished": "2011-05-15T05:42:11.017Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "kashhorn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've made this for years using pepper jack instead of cheddar cheese. Gives it a little kick! I also put it in the small crock pot. Delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2016-02-06T14:01:59.087Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sconi"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Love this dip and its great for get-togethers! I usually put mine in the oven at 250 for ten minutes or until the cheese is melted and the chili starts to bubble. I also use mozzarealla shredded cheese and serve with Frito's big scoops. There's never any left by the end of the night!",
            "datePublished": "2008-09-11T09:37:47.693Z"
          },
          {
